  "description": "PENVIQ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H120 Co2 Er4 N2 O32,2(C5 H10 O2),4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.902-4.013 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.21-122.71°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er4Co2(HL)2(μ3-OH)2(piv)10(OH2)2]·2pivalic acid·4H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
